Separate find while checking versions: five packages reported $VERSION 1.003 -- Kubernetes::REST::RemoteError and the four Kubernetes::REST::CLI::Cmd::* classes. They are the only ones sharing a file with another package, and RewriteVersion/BumpVersionAfterRelease run with global = 0, so only the first package per file gets rewritten. Shipped stale in every release since 1.003, 1.105 included. Set to 1.106 in b1051c0; the mechanism is unfixed and will drift again at 1.107 unless the bundle passes global = 1.

Commits: c2d9be2 (encoding), 3061a04 (Encode prereq), b1051c0 (versions).
Version sweep completed package by package, not just file by file: lib/ holds 39 packages across 34 files and all of them read 1.106 (the five stale ones were the only misses). bin/kube_client and bin/kube_watch had no $VERSION at all -- added in be5cd2f, matching the Getty convention for exec scripts, and both plugins already list :ExecFiles among their finders so the line is maintained from here on. Verified against a real build: Kubernetes-REST-1.106 ships 41 $VERSION declarations, every one of them 1.106.
Root cause removed rather than worked around (f476621): the five packages that shared a file now have files of their own -- RemoteError out of Error.pm, the four CLI::Cmd::* out of CLI.pm. With one package per file, 'first $VERSION' and 'only $VERSION' are the same line and no global => 1 is needed anywhere; the dist.ini could not have set it anyway (verified by building with the option in place: META still said global: 0, because Author::GETTY consumes only PluginBundle::Easy and forwards a fixed key list to \@Git::VersionManager).

Worth knowing: 1.105 shipped CLI::Cmd::Get with 1.003 in the code and 1.105 in META -- MetaProvides::Update corrected the metadata while the source stayed stale, so ->VERSION and the PAUSE index disagreed.

Note for callers: Kubernetes::REST::Error no longer drags RemoteError in. A circular use cannot work when the child inherits from the parent -- use runs at compile time, Moo builds attributes at runtime, so the parent is still empty. Catching is unaffected, throwing needs an explicit use.

t/25_one_package_per_file.t now asserts one package and one $VERSION per file across lib/, all matching the main module. dzil test green, 446 tests.
